# =====================================================================
# Release V165 -- revoke Security access when a user is deactivated in Dentally
# =====================================================================
# A user switched off in Dentally (permission level 0) kept their Security.Application_Users row
# and went on being BILLED, while vanishing from the Subscriptions screen -- which filters on
# COALESCE(u.Permission_Level, sp.perm, 1) > 0. So there was no way to stop it: you cannot
# un-subscribe someone the screen does not draw. Found on dev as Kelly Edge, Practice Manager,
# permission 0, last login 2025-03-04, still billed front_office (£6/month) and still appearing on
# the September invoice.
#
# Both sync procs now use the SAME expression as the roster, so the screen and billing agree by
# construction rather than by coincidence.
#
# ==> IT HAD TO GATE BOTH THE DELETE AND THE INSERT. <== A revoke alone would not hold: AppDB still
# carries the user with their access flags set, so the next run's access-holders-only INSERT would
# re-add them, and the row would oscillate every 10 minutes. The same shape of bug V163 fixed.
#
# ==> ABSENCE IS NOT DEACTIVATION. <== Only a user who HAS a Dim_Users row reading 0 is revoked.
# A failed or part-loaded Gold.Dim_Users would otherwise revoke an entire practice's access in a
# single run. The COALESCE default of 1 likewise keeps a NULL Permission_Level -- every row before
# the Bronze.usp_Load_Users *04 backfill -- meaning "assume active". Both defaults fail OPEN on
# purpose: wrongly keeping access for a few minutes is recoverable, wrongly cutting a practice off
# is not.
#
# Support logins are untouched: they have no Gold.Dim_Users row at all (they are inserted straight
# into Security by SQL), so the EXISTS never matches them.
#
# NOTE ON BILLING HISTORY: removing the Security row stops future billing, and because
# usp_Generate_Invoice_Lines draws its user list from Security, a REGENERATED past month would no
# longer include them. That is contained -- billing_run refuses to regenerate a month that holds a
# finalised invoice -- but it is the reason not to regenerate freely.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V165__revoke_access_on_dentally_deactivation.manifest
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Meta.usp_Sync_Access_From_AppDB.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Meta.usp_Sync_Input_From_AppDB.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
